# Packages only the image for ordinary 64-bit PCs (amd64) asks for.
# The format is the one packages.common describes.

# ── the signed boot chain ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# With UEFI Secure Boot on, a PC's firmware starts only programs signed by a
# key it trusts. The chain: the firmware trusts Microsoft's key; Microsoft has
# signed Debian's "shim"; shim trusts Debian's key; Debian has signed GRUB (the
# boot menu) and the kernel. All four come from Debian's archive as they are.
linux-image-amd64       # Debian's kernel, signed by Debian
shim-signed             # the first program the firmware starts, signed by Microsoft for Debian
grub-efi-amd64          # GRUB, the boot menu, and its tools
grub-efi-amd64-signed   # the GRUB program itself, signed by Debian
